// The one MCP server a session is given is our own stdio bridge, never
// anything the request that asked for the session named. The scenario pins the
// name as well as the command: the name is a public contract that appears in
// users' ego rule files, and the command is the only reason a stdio entry is
// safe to send at all — it is the sidecar we ship, not a caller's process.
